overview.body:
Fiscalis is a personal net-worth tracker. To show your net worth, it processes:

- account data: your name, email address, profile picture and sign-in data;
- financial data you connect or enter: bank accounts, balances and transactions, broker accounts, positions and trades, crypto holdings and transactions, loans, precious metals, retirement plans and portfolio history;
- settings: language, display currency, theme, time zone and onboarding progress;
- technical data: IP address, browser, request times and error logs, needed to deliver and secure the service.

We use this data only to provide Fiscalis to you. We do not sell it, use it for advertising or build marketing profiles. Fiscalis has no ads and no analytics or tracking tools.

marketData.body:
Fiscalis fetches public market data on its servers, without sending any personal data:

- precious-metal prices from gold.de;
- currency exchange rates from the European Central Bank;
- economic indicators from the World Bank Open Data API.

The world map is different: your browser loads map tiles directly from CARTO (CartoDB Inc., USA), which receives your IP address and browser details to deliver them, and the World Map page can query the World Bank API (api.worldbank.org) from your browser. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (our interest in showing the map and data you asked for). CARTO’s privacy policy: https://carto.com/privacy

cookies.body:
Fiscalis uses only cookies that are strictly necessary for the service, so no consent banner is required (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG):

- Clerk session cookies (for example __session and __client_uat) keep you signed in;
- fiscalis-locale remembers the language you chose (1 year);
- fiscalis-tz stores your time zone so dates are shown correctly (1 year);
- sidebar_state remembers whether the sidebar is open (7 days).

The theme you pick may also be kept in your browser’s local storage. We use no advertising, analytics or tracking cookies.

rights.body:
You have the right to:

- access the data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR);
- have wrong data corrected (Art. 16);
- have your data deleted (Art. 17);
- restrict processing (Art. 18);
- receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20);
- object to processing based on our legitimate interests (Art. 21);
- withdraw any consent you gave, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3)).

To use any of these rights, email {email}. We answer within one month.

acceptableUse.body:
Do not misuse Fiscalis. In particular, do not:

- try to access other users’ data or bypass security;
- overload the service, scrape it or use API keys beyond normal personal use;
- use Fiscalis for anything unlawful.

We may suspend accounts that break these rules.
